  "notes": [
    "Capability = weighted mean over benchmark FAMILIES. Weights are relative and are",
    "renormalised over the families a model actually reports.",
    "A family scores exactly ONE benchmark - its first available member - so two",
    "incomparable versions of the same benchmark can never be blended.",
    "A model is scored only if it reports at least `minFamilies` families AND at least",
    "one family listed in `core`. Everything else stays unscored and is never routed",
    "by capability (missing evidence must not renormalise into a high score).",
    "`advisory` numbers are recorded for humans and NEVER feed the score.",
    "terminalBench scores TB2.1 alone: it is the version every model in this cohort",
    "reports. TB4.0 and TB3.0 live under `advisory` because BenchLandscape forbids",
    "mixing TB 2.x with 4.x, and TB3.0 ordering contradicts TB2.1 (kimi-k3: 88.3 on",
    "TB2.1 vs 17.4 on TB3.0). When the cohort moves to TB4.0, change the single",
    "member in `families.terminalBench.members` - never add a second version."
  ],
